"Scope" is a simple software emulation of an oscilloscope.  It
graphically displays voltage as a function of time; the input is via a
sound card using the kernel sound device /dev/dsp. The svgalib library
is used to implement a real-time display.

I have just uploaded this to sunsite.unc.edu. It's in
/pub/Linux/Incoming, but should be moved soon to
/pub/Linux/apps/graphics/scope-0.1.tar.gz.

To run it, you need VGA graphics, the svgalib library, a soundcard, and
the Linux kernel sound drivers.

This is the first release and should be considered ALPHA.  It was
designed more for amusement than as a useful tool.  Distribution
includes source, makefile, and man page.

Jeff

