Heia,

I recently uploaded my callback for Linux package. What it does? It allows you
to call up your Linux box, and request to be called back at a given phone
number. Besides cutting down the phone bill, it's a security thing: only
allowed phone numbers can be called back and hence no-one besides a given set
of "safe" phones can connect in.

Callback comes in two files: callback-1.20.tar.gz and callback.lsm. The
primary site is:
	beatrix.icce.rug.nl, directory pub/unix
Callback will furthermore appear on tsx and sunsite, though I don't know when
the sysops will move the files to the appropriate places (now the files are in
tsx-11.mit.edu:/incoming, sunsite.unc.edu:/pub/Linux/Incoming).

The archive callback-1.20.tar.gz contains also a useful doc file, which may
come in handy if you want to play with the modem.

Cheers,
