It's now been almost 6 months since the initial posting on
comp.os.linux.announce about the Linux Counter.
In the meantime, the counter has been drastically changed, it has
counted more than 5.000 users, and has gained the ability to
register much more information than a simple count.

The intent of the counter is:

- To place a lower limit on estimates of the number of Linux users
  in the world
- To provide some information about what kinds of systems Linux is
  running on
- To provide some names of people using Linux, if the persons want it.

NO information about individuals is EVER passed out of the counter,
except the name, E-mail address and location of those people who have
requested it (by marking "May-publish: yes" in a //PERSON entry).

To register, send E-mail to linux-counter@uninett.no, writing
"I use Linux at home" or "I use Linux at work" or "I use Linux at school"
in the SUBJECT field, or follow the more detailed instructions below.

At this moment (Thu Apr 21 10:04:36 MET DST 1994), the Linux Counter
has counted 5711 users, entered by 5144 people.
688 machine configurations are recorded, 475 names are publicly listed.

All reports are avaialble by anonymous FTP from aun.uninett.no,
directory pub/misc/linux-counter.

The list of countries where Linux is used, which is part of the "short"
report, is included below.

After this, the helpfile for the Linux Counter follows.


